    "q-111028": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111028",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${n}^{2}\\sqrt{27n}+\\sqrt{48{n}^{5}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}\\sqrt{27n}+\\sqrt{48{n}^{5}} & = \\\\ {n}^{2}\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3n}+\\sqrt{16{n}^{4}\\cdot 3n} & = \\\\ {n}^{2}\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3n}+\\sqrt{16{n}^{4}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3n} & = \\\\ 3{n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n}+4{n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine the like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n}+4{n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n} & = \\\\ (3+4){n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n} & = \\\\ 7{n}^{2}\\sqrt{3n}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
